I implemented option A for #1199 and committed it as cd9bfb9a. config show and config get now print *** for the value of any key yoyo doesn't read. The key's name and the "is not a key yoyo reads" warning (with its did-you-mean) still print. fmt, clippy with -D warnings and the full cargo test all pass.

How it decides. I added config_secret::is_masked_key(key): a key is masked if its name looks like a credential (is_secret_key, unchanged) or if it isn't a key yoyo reads. "Reads" is checked by config_unknown_keys::is_top_level_key, the same check the unknown-key warning uses, so the masking and the warning can't disagree about which keys are unknown. All four places that print config values use it: config show, both branches of config get, and the note about a key set in a config file yoyo doesn't load.

Before → after:

| Key | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| model = "claude-x" | shown | shown |
| max_tokens = 8000 | shown | shown (the #1194 case doesn't regress) |
| api_key = "sk-abc" | *** | *** |
| openai = "sk-abc" | shown | *** |
| dsn = "postgres://u:pw@h/db" | shown | *** |
| modle = "claude-x" | shown | ***, and the warning still suggests model |
| allw under [permissions] | not shown | not shown (only top-level keys are displayed); warning unchanged |

Checks:
• The two new display tests failed on the code before the change, with openai, dsn and modle printed raw.
• A third test checks that, for every key yoyo reads plus stripe_sk and a hook, "masked as unknown" matches exactly "the warning names this key".
• To prove the tests can fail, I temporarily replaced the unknown-key half of is_masked_key with false and all three went red. The break and the restore ran in one command, and a grep confirmed the marker was gone afterwards.
• On the freshly built binary (built 12:48:16), yoyo config show on the test file never printed sk-abc or pw@, and yoyo config get openai printed openai = ***.

Cost: to see the raw text of a key yoyo doesn't read, you now have to open the file.

Other changes:
• src/commands_config.rs went from 2015 to 2016 lines, still inside the module-size grace band (it only warns).
• I updated the /config show row in docs/src/usage/commands.md.
• The commit body includes the decision paragraph, these rows, and the file:function that decides "unknown".
